      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Georg Thieme Verlag KG Stuttgart New York.",
        "AbstractText": "Renal hypertension can occur with unilateral ureteropelvic junction obstruction and consecutive hydronephrosis. It is rarely the main symptom, normally in adults flank pain is in the foreground. We report a case of renal hypertension with ureteropelvic junction obstruction successfully corrected by laparoscopic pyeloplasty and discuss the pathophysiology."
